exercises.solution:
```python
def flip(p):
    x, y = p
    return (-x, y)


def quarter_turn(p):
    x, y = p
    return (-y, x)
```

Flipping twice changes the sign of `x` twice, which brings it back. Two quarter turns give `(-x, -y)`, a half turn, and four give `(x, y)` again.
